# Secrets

- **1Password is the single source of truth** for every secret on every surface. Never commit a
  literal secret value, and never commit an `ops_…` Service-Account token.
- **`.env.op`** is git-tracked and holds `op://<vault>/<item>/<field>` references ONLY (safe to
  commit — structural metadata, not secrets). **`.env` / `.env.local`** hold RESOLVED values and
  stay gitignored.
- **MCP placeholder syntax never changes** (INVARIANT 2): `.cursor/mcp.json` keeps `${env:VAR}`;
  the generated root `.mcp.json` keeps `${VAR:-}`. Only secret *delivery* changes — anyone
  "upgrading" a placeholder to `op://` is wrong.
- **Delivery per surface** (handled OUTSIDE the repo; you never invoke it):
  - local — chezmoi renders the launchctl cache from 1Password (biometric `op`).
  - Claude cloud — SessionStart `.claude/hooks/bootstrap-secrets.sh` runs `op inject` →
    `$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE` (the only `op inject` in the project domain; fail-open, no token → no-op).
  - GitHub Actions — `op inject` via `sa-ci` (1Password CLI).
- **Add a new secret**: add the VAR name to `.env.example` and a `op://` line to `.env.op`. Never
  paste the value. Locate an existing one with `~/Dev/_shared/_scripts/resolve-secret.sh <VAR>`.
